            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Cisco earnings, Fed, House votes on shutdown bill: What to Watch",
            "description": "<p>Market Domination Overtime host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> previews several of the biggest stories to come tomorrow, Wednesday, November 12, including corporate earnings results from companies like Cisco Systems (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CSCO\">CSCO</a>), FanDuel-parent company Flutter Entertainment (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/FLUT\">FLUT</a>), and Tencent Music Entertainment (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TME\">TME</a>); commentary from an array of top Federal Reserve officials; and US House lawmakers are expected to vote on the spending bill tomorrow that could possibly end the government shutdown.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance's Invest conference kicks off at 8:00 A.M. this Thursday, November 13, a day filled with high-profile interviews and panel discussions.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
